# [NMRG](../wg/nmrg.html)

## Summary

The Network Management Research Group (NMRG) met at IETF 127 to discuss research progress in intent-based networking (IBN), AI-driven network management architectures, network digital twins (NDT), and priority-based transport control for LLM streaming inference traffic. The session included four technical presentations, an update on document progression to Research Group Last Call (RGLC), and requests for research group adoption.

## Key Discussion Points

### Chairs' Introduction
* Presentation: [1 - Chairs slides](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-nmrg-sessa-1-chairs-slides-00)
* Presenter: Jérôme François

* Jérôme François opened the meeting and presented the IETF Note Well, IPR disclosure policy, privacy rules, code of conduct, and audio/video recording disclosures.
* Reintegrated the distinction between the IRTF (focusing on longer-term research issues) and the IETF (focusing on shorter-term engineering and standards creation).
